traceability.evidence:
Implementation rule present and story-linked:
- File: src/rules/valid-req-reference.ts
- Header JSDoc:
  "Rule to validate @req annotation references refer to existing requirements in story files"
  "@story docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md"
  "@req REQ-DEEP-PARSE - Parse comments and extract story/requirement metadata"
  "@req REQ-DEEP-MATCH - Match @req annotations to story file requirements"
  "@req REQ-DEEP-CACHE - Cache requirement IDs per story file for efficient validation"

Core deep-validation logic:
- Function validateReqLine(...):
  - Extracts reqId from the @req line:
    const parts = line.split(/\s+/);
    const reqId = parts[1];
  - Resolves storyPath safely, rejecting traversal/absolute paths:
    if (storyPath.includes("..") || path.isAbsolute(storyPath)) { context.report({ messageId: "invalidPath" ... }); return; }
    const resolvedStoryPath = path.resolve(cwd, storyPath);
    if (!resolvedStoryPath.startsWith(cwd + path.sep) && resolvedStoryPath !== cwd) { context.report({ messageId: "invalidPath" ... }); return; }
  - Caches parsed requirements per story file (REQ-DEEP-CACHE):
    const reqCache = new Map<string, Set>();
    if (!reqCache.has(resolvedStoryPath)) {
      const content = fs.readFileSync(resolvedStoryPath, "utf8");
      const found = new Set();
      const regex = /REQ-[A-Z0-9-]+/g;
      let match: RegExpExecArray | null;
      while ((match = regex.exec(content)) !== null) {
        found.add(match[0]);
      }
      reqCache.set(resolvedStoryPath, found);
    }
  - Deep requirement existence check (REQ-DEEP-MATCH):
    const reqSet = reqCache.get(resolvedStoryPath)!;
    if (!reqSet.has(reqId)) {
      context.report({
        node: comment as any,
        messageId: "reqMissing",
        data: { reqId, storyPath },
      });
    }

Requirement format & section handling (REQ-DEEP-FORMAT, REQ-DEEP-SECTION):
- Uses a single regex /REQ-[A-Z0-9-]+/g over the entire markdown file content, so IDs are detected regardless of:
  - Placement in bullet lists, numbered lists, acceptance criteria checkboxes, or plain requirement sections.
- Example fixtures and stories show different formats all compatible with this strategy:
  - docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md contains requirements as bullets: "- **REQ-DEEP-PARSE**: ..." etc.
  - tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md:
    "- REQ-BULLET-LIST - a requirement in bullet list format"

Annotation and story-path integration (integration with existing parsing/file validation):
- The rule walks all comments once per file and threads the last seen @story through subsequent @req lines:
  - programListener(context):
    const sourceCode = context.getSourceCode();
    const cwd = process.cwd();
    const reqCache = new Map<string, Set>();
    let rawStoryPath: string | null = null;
    return function Program() {
      const comments = sourceCode.getAllComments() || [];
      comments.forEach((comment: any) => {
        rawStoryPath = handleComment({
          comment,
          context,
          cwd,
          reqCache,
          rawStoryPath,
        });
      });
    };
- handleComment splits each JSDoc/line comment into lines, strips comment markers, and for each line delegates to handleAnnotationLine.
- handleAnnotationLine:
  - If line starts with "@story", it calls extractStoryPath(comment) and updates the shared storyPath.
  - If line starts with "@req", it calls validateReqLine(...) using the current storyPath.
=> This wires deep requirement checking onto the existing annotation format conventions established in earlier stories.

Error messages and error handling (REQ-DEEP-ERROR + 007.0 dependency):
- meta.messages in src/rules/valid-req-reference.ts:
  - reqMissing: "Requirement '{{reqId}}' not found in '{{storyPath}}'"
    - JSDoc links back to 010.0 and 007.0 with:
      "@req REQ-ERROR-SPECIFIC - Provide specific diagnostics when a referenced requirement ID cannot be found in a story"
      "@req REQ-ERROR-CONTEXT - Include both the missing requirement ID and the story path in the message"
      "@req REQ-ERROR-CONSISTENCY - Use a consistent message template for requirement lookup failures"
  - invalidPath: "Invalid story path '{{storyPath}}'"
- FS and parsing robustness:
  - If fs.readFileSync throws (missing file, permission error, etc.), the rule catches and sets an empty Set in the cache:
    try { ... } catch { reqCache.set(resolvedStoryPath, new Set()); }
  - This prevents crashes on malformed or inaccessible story files; such cases degrade gracefully to "requirement not found" diagnostics, satisfying the "gracefully handles" criterion (no uncaught exceptions during linting).

Tests specifically for deep validation behavior:
- File: tests/rules/valid-req-reference.test.ts
- JSDoc header:
  "Tests for: docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md"
  "@story docs/stories/010.0-DEV-DEEP-VALIDATION.story.md"
  "@req REQ-DEEP-PARSE - Verify valid-req-reference rule enforces existing requirement content"
- Uses ESLint RuleTester:
  const ruleTester = new RuleTester({ languageOptions: { parserOptions: { ecmaVersion: 2020 } }, } as any);
  ruleTester.run("valid-req-reference", rule, { ... });
- Valid cases:
  1) "[REQ-DEEP-PARSE] valid requirement reference existing in story file"
     code:
       // @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
       // @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE
     -> Confirms deep matching against an actual story requirement in docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md.
  2) "[REQ-DEEP-BULLET] valid bullet list requirement existing in bullet story fixture"
     code:
       // @story tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md
       // @req REQ-BULLET-LIST
     -> Confirms bullet-list formats are correctly parsed and matched.
- Invalid cases:
  1) "[REQ-DEEP-MATCH] missing requirement in story file"
     code:
       // @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
       // @req REQ-NON-EXISTENT
     errors: [ { messageId: "reqMissing", data: { reqId: "REQ-NON-EXISTENT", storyPath: "docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md" } } ]
  2) "[REQ-DEEP-PARSE] disallow path traversal in story path"
     code:
       // @story ../docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
       // @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE
     errors: [ { messageId: "invalidPath", data: { storyPath: "../docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md" } } ]
  3) "[REQ-DEEP-PARSE] disallow absolute path in story path"
     code:
       // @story /absolute/path/docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
       // @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE
     errors: [ { messageId: "invalidPath", data: { storyPath: "/absolute/path/docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md" } } ]
  4) "[REQ-DEEP-BULLET] missing bullet list requirement in bullet story fixture"
     code:
       // @story tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md
       // @req REQ-MISSING-BULLET
     errors: [ { messageId: "reqMissing", data: { reqId: "REQ-MISSING-BULLET", storyPath: "tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md" } } ]

Story fixtures containing real requirements used by the rule:
- docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md contains "**REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE**" etc.
- tests/fixtures/story_bullet.md contains "- REQ-BULLET-LIST - a requirement in bullet list format" and "- REQ-ANOTHER - another requirement".

Plugin registration (integration with existing plugin structure):
- File: src/index.ts
  const RULE_NAMES = [
    "require-story-annotation",
    "require-req-annotation",
    "require-branch-annotation",
